{
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed dwelling, because of its poor street presence and of it being an incongruous and inappropriate back-land development in a residential garden, would cause harm to the character and appearance of the site and surrounding area, contrary to Local Plan policies CC1, CC2 and the intent of the NPPF and the Housing Design Standards LPG. It would also represent inappropriate development within the curtilage of an existing house while conflicting with other Development Plan policies, rendering it unacceptable in principle and contrary to Local Plan policy SC1.",
    "Reason : 2 - The subdivision of the existing site would result in insufficient and poor-quality private amenity space for both the existing and new dwellings at the application site, contrary to Local Plan policies SC1, CC1, CC2 and SC5.",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposed new dwelling, by reason of its siting, proximity, and improper design, would harm the living conditions of the main house at No.52 and its neighbour at No.54, contrary to Local Plan policies CC2, SC7 and EQ5. ",
    "Reason : 4 - The application has failed to demonstrate that carbon savings have been maximised at all steps of the energy hierarchy, or commit to offset any residual emissions via a carbon offset payment. Consequently, it fails to comply with Local Plan policy EQ2.  ",
    "Reason : 5 - The application has failed to provide sufficient information to demonstrate that the development would deliver appropriate transport and servicing provisions, contrary to Local Plan policies EC2.",
    "Reason : 6 - The application has failed to provide adequate information to comply with the requirements of Biodiversity Net Gain (BNG) under Schedule 7A of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, and Local Plan policy GB7. It also fails to identify or set out measures to protect existing ecology and trees on site or in the site's vicinity. "
  ],
